IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `oapa-nouns`
IMPORT `oapa-danger-bodily-harm`

-- Offences against the Person Act 1861 -- TESTS for oapa-danger-bodily-harm.l4
-- (sections 17 to 25).  Every expected value was decided from the section's text before
-- the assertion was written, and is stated beside it.  OF is positional: each group of
-- cases has a ruler naming the columns in DECLARE order.

§ `Tests: sections 17 to 25`

§§ `Section 17`

-- unlawfully, maliciously, limb 1 (impeding a person saving their own life), limb 2
-- (impeding a person saving the life of such a person)
`s17 limb 1` MEANS `Conduct under section 17` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s17 limb 2` MEANS `Conduct under section 17` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s17 neither limb` MEANS `Conduct under section 17` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s17 not unlawful` MEANS `Conduct under section 17` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s17 not malicious` MEANS `Conduct under section 17` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 17: impeding a person endeavouring to save their life from shipwreck` `s17 limb 1`
#ASSERT `s 17: impeding a person endeavouring to save their life from shipwreck` `s17 limb 2`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17: impeding a person endeavouring to save their life from shipwreck` `s17 neither limb`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17: impeding a person endeavouring to save their life from shipwreck` `s17 not unlawful`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 17: impeding a person endeavouring to save their life from shipwreck` `s17 not malicious`)
#ASSERT `s 17: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `s 17: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` `for life`

§§ `Section 18`

-- unlawfully, maliciously, wounded, caused grievous bodily harm, intent to do grievous
-- bodily harm, intent to resist or prevent lawful apprehension or detainer
`s18 wound, intent GBH` MEANS `Conduct under section 18` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s18 wound, intent resist` MEANS `Conduct under section 18` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s18 cause GBH, intent GBH` MEANS `Conduct under section 18` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s18 cause GBH, intent resist` MEANS `Conduct under section 18` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s18 wound, no intent` MEANS `Conduct under section 18` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s18 intent, no wound and no GBH` MEANS `Conduct under section 18` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`s18 not unlawful` MEANS `Conduct under section 18` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s18 not malicious` MEANS `Conduct under section 18` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

-- the four combinations of conduct (wound / cause GBH) and intent (GBH / resist)
#ASSERT `s 18: wounding or causing grievous bodily harm, with intent` `s18 wound, intent GBH`
#ASSERT `s 18: wounding or causing grievous bodily harm, with intent` `s18 wound, intent resist`
#ASSERT `s 18: wounding or causing grievous bodily harm, with intent` `s18 cause GBH, intent GBH`
#ASSERT `s 18: wounding or causing grievous bodily harm, with intent` `s18 cause GBH, intent resist`
-- either part missing
#ASSERT NOT (`s 18: wounding or causing grievous bodily harm, with intent` `s18 wound, no intent`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 18: wounding or causing grievous bodily harm, with intent` `s18 intent, no wound and no GBH`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 18: wounding or causing grievous bodily harm, with intent` `s18 not unlawful`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 18: wounding or causing grievous bodily harm, with intent` `s18 not malicious`)
#ASSERT `s 18: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `s 18: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` `for life`

§§ `Section 19`

#ASSERT `s 19: blank in this text` EQUALS "Section 19 shows only its number and a row of dots; there is nothing to encode."

§§ `Section 20`

-- unlawfully, maliciously, wounded another person, inflicted grievous bodily harm,
-- used a weapon or instrument
`s20 wounded without a weapon` MEANS `Conduct under section 20` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s20 wounded with a weapon` MEANS `Conduct under section 20` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s20 inflicted GBH without a weapon` MEANS `Conduct under section 20` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s20 weapon but no wound and no GBH` MEANS `Conduct under section 20` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s20 not unlawful` MEANS `Conduct under section 20` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s20 not malicious` MEANS `Conduct under section 20` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

-- "either with or without any weapon or instrument": the weapon changes nothing.
#ASSERT `s 20: wounding or inflicting grievous bodily harm` `s20 wounded without a weapon`
#ASSERT `s 20: wounding or inflicting grievous bodily harm` `s20 wounded with a weapon`
#ASSERT `s 20: wounding or inflicting grievous bodily harm` `s20 inflicted GBH without a weapon`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 20: wounding or inflicting grievous bodily harm` `s20 weapon but no wound and no GBH`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 20: wounding or inflicting grievous bodily harm` `s20 not unlawful`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 20: wounding or inflicting grievous bodily harm` `s20 not malicious`)
#ASSERT `s 20: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS misdemeanor
-- "penal servitude . . .": the dots hide the term, so the text states none.
#ASSERT `s 20: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` `for a term the text does not state`

§§ `Section 21`

-- attempted to choke, suffocate or strangle; attempted to render insensible by means
-- calculated to choke etc.; intent to enable; intent to assist
`s21 choke, intent to enable` MEANS `Conduct under section 21` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s21 choke, intent to assist` MEANS `Conduct under section 21` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s21 render insensible, intent to enable` MEANS `Conduct under section 21` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s21 render insensible, intent to assist` MEANS `Conduct under section 21` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s21 intent but no attempt` MEANS `Conduct under section 21` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`s21 attempt but no intent` MEANS `Conduct under section 21` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 21: attempting to choke or render insensible, to commit an indictable offence` `s21 choke, intent to enable`
#ASSERT `s 21: attempting to choke or render insensible, to commit an indictable offence` `s21 choke, intent to assist`
#ASSERT `s 21: attempting to choke or render insensible, to commit an indictable offence` `s21 render insensible, intent to enable`
#ASSERT `s 21: attempting to choke or render insensible, to commit an indictable offence` `s21 render insensible, intent to assist`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 21: attempting to choke or render insensible, to commit an indictable offence` `s21 intent but no attempt`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 21: attempting to choke or render insensible, to commit an indictable offence` `s21 attempt but no intent`)
#ASSERT `s 21: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `s 21: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` `for life`

§§ `Section 22`

-- unlawfully, applied or administered (or caused to be taken), attempted to,
-- intent to enable, intent to assist
`s22 applied, intent to enable` MEANS `Conduct under section 22` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s22 attempted only, intent to assist` MEANS `Conduct under section 22` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s22 not unlawful` MEANS `Conduct under section 22` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s22 neither applied nor attempted` MEANS `Conduct under section 22` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`s22 applied, no intent` MEANS `Conduct under section 22` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 22: administering a stupefying drug, to commit an indictable offence` `s22 applied, intent to enable`
#ASSERT `s 22: administering a stupefying drug, to commit an indictable offence` `s22 attempted only, intent to assist`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 22: administering a stupefying drug, to commit an indictable offence` `s22 not unlawful`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 22: administering a stupefying drug, to commit an indictable offence` `s22 neither applied nor attempted`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 22: administering a stupefying drug, to commit an indictable offence` `s22 applied, no intent`)
#ASSERT `s 22: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `s 22: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` `for life`

§§ `Section 23`

-- unlawfully, maliciously, administered, thereby endangered life, thereby inflicted GBH
`s23 endangered life` MEANS `Conduct under section 23` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s23 inflicted GBH` MEANS `Conduct under section 23` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s23 administered but no result` MEANS `Conduct under section 23` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s23 result but not administered` MEANS `Conduct under section 23` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`s23 not unlawful` MEANS `Conduct under section 23` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s23 not malicious` MEANS `Conduct under section 23` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 23: administering poison so as to endanger life or inflict grievous bodily harm` `s23 endangered life`
#ASSERT `s 23: administering poison so as to endanger life or inflict grievous bodily harm` `s23 inflicted GBH`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23: administering poison so as to endanger life or inflict grievous bodily harm` `s23 administered but no result`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23: administering poison so as to endanger life or inflict grievous bodily harm` `s23 result but not administered`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23: administering poison so as to endanger life or inflict grievous bodily harm` `s23 not unlawful`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23: administering poison so as to endanger life or inflict grievous bodily harm` `s23 not malicious`)
#ASSERT `s 23: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS felony
-- "any term not exceeding ten years": 120 months
#ASSERT `s 23: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` (`for a term not exceeding` 120)

§§ `Section 24`

-- unlawfully, maliciously, administered, intent to injure, intent to aggrieve, intent to annoy
`s24 intent to injure` MEANS `Conduct under section 24` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s24 intent to aggrieve` MEANS `Conduct under section 24` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s24 intent to annoy` MEANS `Conduct under section 24` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s24 no intent` MEANS `Conduct under section 24` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s24 intent but not administered` MEANS `Conduct under section 24` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s24 not unlawful` MEANS `Conduct under section 24` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s24 not malicious` MEANS `Conduct under section 24` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 24: administering poison with intent to injure, aggrieve or annoy` `s24 intent to injure`
#ASSERT `s 24: administering poison with intent to injure, aggrieve or annoy` `s24 intent to aggrieve`
#ASSERT `s 24: administering poison with intent to injure, aggrieve or annoy` `s24 intent to annoy`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 24: administering poison with intent to injure, aggrieve or annoy` `s24 no intent`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 24: administering poison with intent to injure, aggrieve or annoy` `s24 intent but not administered`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 24: administering poison with intent to injure, aggrieve or annoy` `s24 not unlawful`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 24: administering poison with intent to injure, aggrieve or annoy` `s24 not malicious`)
#ASSERT `s 24: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `s 24: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` `for a term the text does not state`

§§ `Section 25`

-- tried for the section 23 felony, jury not satisfied of it, jury satisfied of the
-- section 24 misdemeanor
`s25 the alternative verdict is open` MEANS `Trial under section 25` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s25 jury is satisfied of the felony` MEANS `Trial under section 25` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s25 jury is not satisfied of the misdemeanor` MEANS `Trial under section 25` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s25 not tried for the section 23 felony` MEANS `Trial under section 25` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE

#ASSERT `s 25: the jury may acquit of the section 23 felony and find the person guilty of the section 24 misdemeanor` `s25 the alternative verdict is open`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 25: the jury may acquit of the section 23 felony and find the person guilty of the section 24 misdemeanor` `s25 jury is satisfied of the felony`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 25: the jury may acquit of the section 23 felony and find the person guilty of the section 24 misdemeanor` `s25 jury is not satisfied of the misdemeanor`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 25: the jury may acquit of the section 23 felony and find the person guilty of the section 24 misdemeanor` `s25 not tried for the section 23 felony`)
-- then punished as for the section 24 misdemeanor (penal servitude, term not stated)
#ASSERT `s 25: the sentences open after an alternative verdict` `s25 the alternative verdict is open` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` `for a term the text does not state`
#ASSERT `s 25: the sentences open after an alternative verdict` `s25 jury is satisfied of the felony` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 25: the sentences open after an alternative verdict` `s25 not tried for the section 23 felony` EQUALS EMPTY
